0a9 2016. Government of Tamil Nadu. All rights reserved.  \n \n \nYou will be redirected to the service page on the Tamil Nadu e-District Web Portal.  \n \nSTEP 8:Click on Proceed to continue. \n \n \nApplicant Search form will appear. Search can be performed using the following options: \n \n\uf0b7 Applicants CAN Number \n\uf0b7 Applicant Name \nClick on the Service \nName \nClick on Proceed Tamil Nadu e-District Application User Manual  \n \u00a9 20", "16. Government of Tamil Nadu. All rights reserved.  \n\uf0b7 Applicant Father Name \n\uf0b7 Applicant Mobile Number \n\uf0b7 Applicant Email Id \n\uf0b7 Applicant Date Of Birth \n \nThe green asterisksignifies that the available search options are optional mandatory. \n \nAn applicant can apply for the Residence Certificateprovided he/she is having a unique CAN number. \n \nIf the applicant doesn\u2019t have a unique CAN Number, he must register for CAN to access the application form \nforResidenceCertificate.  \n7.1. Registering f", "or CAN (Citizen Access Number) \nSTEP 1:Click on the \u2018Click here\u2019 link to apply for CAN Registration. \n \n \nThe below figure shows the CAN Registration form.  \n \nSTEP 2:Fill up all mandatory details in the form prescribed format.  \n \n \nClick to apply for CAN \nRegistration Tamil Nadu e-District Application User Manual  \n \u00a9 2016. Government of Tamil Nadu. All rights reserved.  \n \n \nSTEP 3:Click on Register to submit form. \n \nFill up the CAN \nRegistration form \nClick to \nsubmit form Tamil Nadu e-Dist", "rict Application User Manual  \n \u00a9 2016. Government of Tamil Nadu. All rights reserved.  \n \nNote: You would be required to generate and verify OTP before submitting the form. \n \n \n \nOn successful CAN Registration, the CAN Number will be shown. \n \n \nTheapplicant may now proceed with applying for the Residence Certificateby clicking on the Proceed button. \n7.2. Applying for Residence Certificate \nIf the applicant is having a unique CAN Number his/her record will be shown in the search results. \nCli", "ck to apply for the \nCertificate Tamil Nadu e-District Application User Manual  \n \u00a9 2016. Government of Tamil Nadu. All rights reserved.  \n \n \nSTEP 1:Select the record by clicking on the option button against the desired record. \n \nSTEP 2:Click on Proceed. \n \nCAN details of the applicant may be modified by clicking on the Edit CAN Detail button. \n \nThe Save as New option allows you to save the same CAN Number with different applicant details. \n \n \n7.2.1. Filling upResidence Certificateform \nSECT", "ION1:Applicant Details \n \nApplicant details will appear pre-filled in the form. These details are non-editable. Enter Ration Card No. \n \nSearch results \nClick to select record \nClick to proceed Tamil Nadu e-District Application User Manual  \n \u00a9 2016. Government of Tamil Nadu. All rights reserved.  \n \n \nSECTION 2: Current Address \n \nApplicant\u2019s current address details will appear pre-filled in the form. These details are non-editable. \n \n \n \nSECTION 3: Permanent Address \n \nApplicant\u2019s permanent a", "ddress details will appear pre-filled in the form. These details are non-editable. \n \n \n \nSECTION 4:Contact Details \n \nApplicant\u2019s contact details will appear pre-filled in the form. These details are non-editable. \n \nTamil Nadu e-District Application User Manual  \n \u00a9 2016. Government of Tamil Nadu. All rights reserved.  \n \n \nSECTION 5:Address Details of the applicant in descending chronological order  \n \nEnter address details of the applicant (from 1 to 5 years) in descending chronological orde", "r. Total years will be \nshown at the bottom of the section. \n \n \nClick on Submit. The \u2018Cancel\u2019 button closes the application form. \n \n \n \n \nNext screen will show a list of required documents.  \n \nAttach the documents in prescribed file size and file type. Uploaded documents will be shown at the bottom.You \nmay remove any uploaded document using the cross sign. \n \nPlease note that the \u2018Upload\u2019 button will appear once you browse and add a document. \n \nClick to add record \nEnter addressdetails \nAdd", "ed record \nClick to submit \nformdetails Tamil Nadu e-District Application User Manual  \n \u00a9 2016. Government of Tamil Nadu. All rights reserved.  \n \n \nAfter uploading the documents, click on \u2018Make Payment\u2019. \n \n \n \nPayments page will appear. Amount payable (Total Fees) will be shown on screen. Click on Confirm Payment. \n \nSelect a document \nEnter document no. \nBrowse and upload \ndocument Uploaded documents \nClick to make payment Tamil Nadu e-District Application User Manual  \n \u00a9 2016. Government o", "f Tamil Nadu. All rights reserved.  \n \n \nAcknowledgement receipt will be shown. \n \nClick on Print Receipt to download/print the receipt. \n \n \n \n \nThe below figure shows the preview of the acknowledgement receipt. \n \nClick to confirm \npayment \nClick to print receipt Tamil Nadu e-District Application User Manual  \n \u00a9 2016. Government of Tamil Nadu. All rights reserved.  \n \nTamil Nadu e-District Application User Manual  \n \u00a9 2016. Government of Tamil Nadu. All rights reserved.  \n \nPlease Note: \n \nAf", "ter submission (clicking on the Submit button), the application will be saved as draft. You can find draft \napplications under the Saved Application section and upload documents or make payment as required. \n \n \n \nSubmitted applications can be viewed under the Submitted Application section. \n \n \n \nThe current status of an application can be checked from the Check Status section. \n \nTamil Nadu e-District Application User Manual  \n \u00a9 2016. Government of Tamil Nadu. All rights reserved.  \n \n \nAckno", "wledgement receipts can be re-printed from the Reprint Receipt section. \n \n \n7.3. Downloading Certificate \nOnce the application is approved and digitally signed, the Residence Certificatecan be downloaded from the \nOperator\u2019s desk and handed over to the applicant. \n \nSTEP 1:Click on Check Status. \n \nSTEP 2:Enter Application Number. \n \nSTEP 3:Click on Search. \n \nTamil Nadu e-District Application User Manual  \n \u00a9 2016. Government of Tamil Nadu. All rights reserved.  \n \n \nThe application will show ", "up. \n  \nSTEP 4:Click on Download certificate link. \n \n \n \nThe certificate will be downloaded. \n \nThe below figure shows the preview of the Residence Certificate. \n \nClick to download \ncertificate \nClick on Search \nEnter Application \nNo. \nClick on Check Status Tamil Nadu e-District Application User Manual  \n \u00a9 2016. Government of Tamil Nadu. All rights reserved.  \n \n \n \nTamil Nadu e-District Application User Manual  \n \u00a9 2016. Government of Tamil Nadu. All rights reserved.  \n8. Disclaimer \nThis Us", "er manual is prepared as per the existing application; however actual screen shots may vary for few cases. \n ", "Residence Certificate \u2013 Structured Information\nService Details\nService ID: 75\nDepartment: Revenue Administration\nService Name: Residence Certificate\nAccess Type: Operator\nOnline Availability: Yes\nService Charge (INR): 60\nThis document contains cleanly structured and standardized information related to the Residence\nCertificate service under Revenue Administration. The tabular service details and document\nrequirements are suitable for use in a Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) model.\nMandatory", " Documents (Required for All Applicants)\nThe following documents must be submitted by every applicant without exception:\n1. Applicant Photograph\n2. Current Address Proof\n3. Self-Declaration of Applicant\nCategory-wise Document Classification\n1. General Citizens\nGeneral citizens may submit any one or more of the following supporting documents, in addition to\nthe mandatory documents:\n\u007f Passport\n\u007f Driving Licence\n\u007f PAN Card\n\u007f Bank / Post Office Passbook with Photograph\n\u007f Smart Card issued by RGI und", "er NPR\n\u007f Health Insurance Smart Card (Ministry of Labour Scheme)\n\u007f Pension Document with Photograph\n\u007f Authenticated Photo Voter Slip issued by Election Authority\n2. Government Employees / Public Representatives\nGovernment employees or elected public representatives may submit the following documents\nalong with the mandatory documents:\n\u007f Service Identity Card issued by Central or State Government\n\u007f Official Identity Cards issued to MPs / MLAs / MLCs\nImportant Notes\n\u007f Mandatory documents are requi", "red for all applicants.\n\u007f Supporting documents vary based on applicant category.\n\u007f Applicants are not required to submit all listed documents, only those applicable.\n", "Residence Certificate \u2013 Service Overview and\nDocument Reasoning\nWhat is the Residence Certificate Service?\nThe Residence Certificate is an official government document issued by the Revenue\nAdministration department to certify that an individual resides at a specific address within a defined\njurisdiction. It is commonly used for accessing government schemes, educational admissions,\nemployment verification, address validation, and legal or administrative purposes.\nWhy Documents are Collected\nDocu", "ments are collected to verify the applicant\u2019s identity, confirm their residential address, and\nprevent misuse or fraudulent claims. Each document serves a specific verification purpose, allowing\nauthorities to make accurate and lawful decisions.\nReasoning Behind Each Document\nApplicant Photograph\nUsed to visually identify the applicant and link the certificate to the correct individual.\nCurrent Address Proof\nConfirms that the applicant is currently residing at the claimed address.\nSelf-Declarati", "on\nActs as a legal statement from the applicant affirming that the provided information is true.\nPassport\nProvides government-issued proof of identity and address with high credibility.\nDriving Licence\nServes as an officially recognized identity and address proof.\nPAN Card\nUsed to validate identity and ensure uniqueness of the applicant.\nBank / Post Office Passbook\nConfirms residence through financial records linked to the applicant.\nSmart Card (RGI/NPR)\nUsed for population registry-based identi", "ty and residence verification.\nHealth Insurance Smart Card\nVerifies identity through government welfare enrollment records.\nPension Document\nConfirms long-term residence and beneficiary status.\nService Identity Card\nValidates employment and official identity of government employees.\nMP/MLA/MLC Identity Card\nConfirms elected representative status and official credentials.\nPhoto Voter Slip\nUsed to verify electoral identity and residential constituency.\nHow This Helps Reasoning-Based User Queries\nB", "y understanding the purpose of each document, the system can explain why a document is\nrequired, suggest alternatives when applicable, and provide transparent reasoning to users asking\nfollow-up questions about eligibility or verification requirements.\n"]
